; ============================================================================
;  SINTAB.INC - the sine, minted once: 256 cells, the whole circle in one
;  byte. Each cell is round(127 * sin(i * 2*pi / 256)), a signed byte:
;  -127..127, so a length multiplied through IMUL and shifted right seven
;  places (/128) comes out in pixels. cos(a) is this same table read at
;  a + 64: a quarter of 256 is a quarter of the circle.
;
;  GENERATED by TOOLS\SinTab (dotnet run --project TOOLS\SinTab -- <path>).
;  Nobody typed these numbers, and nobody in 1988 typed theirs either -
;  the games' hsin and hcos are this table's grown-up kin.
; ============================================================================
